    "body": "You removed the wrong sentence :). We want to get to a world where every enumerated attribute that has an \"invalid value default\" and a \"missing value default\", so in that case the \"Otherwise\" is not necessary.\r\n\r\nBut, we still need to cover cases where neither is defined, in which case there is no state represented. (Or maybe we can go through and add a \"no value\" state to every element, but that'd be a separate effort.)",
